<div id="KRCKey_div" style="display:none;">
The KRC button will "separate" a fairisle stitch pattern for use with double bed jacquard. Double Bed Jacquard is multi-color slip with colors changing every 2 rows. In the following example, the 6 row (even number of rows) fairisle design is "separated" to a 6 color design. Notice the color memo numbers on the separated stitch pattern.

        
            <img src="/challenge/images/v2/103/krc1.jpg">
            
                <img src="/challenge/images/v2/103/krc21.jpg">
            
        

        <br>  If you are new to Double Bed Jacquard, <span class="yellow_highlight">it is highly recommended you use the built-in stitch patterns in the Stitch World book that are already separated.</span>  Patterns 368-394.  Once you get more familiar with this technique you can experiment with your own separations.
        <br>

    </div>


<script language="JavaScript">
    $(".showimage").click(function() {
        $(".optionimage").hide();
        $("#" + $(this).attr('data-show')).show();
        $("#button1").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/1.png');
        $("#button2").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/2.png');
        $("#button3").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/3.png');
        $("#button4").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/4.png');
        $("#button5").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/5.png');
        $("#button6").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/6.png');
        $("#button7").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/7.png');
        $("#button7").attr('src', '/challenge/images/v2/103/7.png');
        $("#" + $(this).attr('data-buttonid')).attr('src', $(this).attr('data-buttoninfo'));
        $("#buttondescrption").html($(this).attr('data-desc'));
        $("#KRCKey_div").hide();
    });


$( ".KRCKey" ).click(function() {
$(".optionimage").hide();
  $('#KRCKey_div').toggle();
});
</script>
